{
  "_doc": "How tools/audio.py drives Kwirk's sound engine. RAM names come from ram.inc. One queue for everything: QueueSound (rst $30) puts an id into wSoundQueue and UpdateSound (once a frame, from the VBlank handler) starts one queued sound per frame. A sound is a header in Sounds of (channel, stream) pairs: channels 0-3 are the music voices, 4-7 the sound effects that take over the same four voices while they play.",
  "init": "InitSound",
  "update": "UpdateSound",
  "_power_on": "InitSound turns the wave DAC on (rNR30 $80); wave RAM starts out as TriangleWave: the music loads it (command $FC on the wave voice) before any wave effect plays, and a wave effect's own $FC does not load anything",
